+.. setting:: redis_backend_credential_provider
+
+.. versionadded:: 5.6
+
+``redis_backend_credential_provider``
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Default: Not configured.
+
+The Redis backend supports credential providers. This value may be either
+a dotted-string path to a :class:`redis.CredentialProvider` subclass, which
+is resolved and instantiated at connection setup time, or a direct instance
+of a ``redis.CredentialProvider`` subclass.
+
+When a credential provider is active, the ``username`` and ``password``
+keys are automatically removed from the connection parameters to avoid
+conflicts.
+
+Passing a value that is neither a valid string path to a
+``CredentialProvider`` subclass nor an actual ``CredentialProvider``
+instance raises :exc:`ValueError`. An unresolvable string path raises
+:exc:`ImportError`.
+
+Example::
+
+    app.conf.redis_backend_credential_provider = 'redis.UsernamePasswordCredentialProvider'
+
